WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:22.393
On Thursday Brooklyn nervously watched the Whales play their first opponent in the play-offs: the Loganville Leopards.

2
00:00:22.394 --> 00:00:29.891
The team started off slowly, but the action picked up in the second half, after Dirk and Jacey rejoined the team.

3
00:00:29.892 --> 00:00:42.969
"Phew," she thought when Dirk scored a three-pointer five seconds before the final buzzer. The Whales won, 59-56.

4
00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:47.133
"Nice win, Whales," Marv said after the game.

5
00:00:47.134 --> 00:00:54.267
"Next we play the Bobcats. And if the Terriers win their next game, we'll face them again in the final game."

6
00:00:54.268 --> 00:01:02.847
"Oh no." Everyone groaned at the thought of playing that team with their giant point guard again.

7
00:01:02.848 --> 00:01:08.917
"We'll practice hard!" Brooklyn said quickly. "We can beat them—Whales Whoosh!"

8
00:01:08.918 --> 00:01:16.259
"Whales Whoosh," a few players echoed, but they didn't sound very enthusiastic.

9
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.057
Brooklyn spent Sunday afternoon trying to study for Monday's history test.

10
00:01:21.058 --> 00:01:29.662
She rearranged her note cards and stared at the sky through her window.

11
00:01:29.663 --> 00:01:34.914
It was a cool March day, but the bright sun made it feel like spring

12
00:01:34.915 --> 00:01:38.160
Brooklyn couldn't stop thinking about the Whales.

13
00:01:38.161 --> 00:01:48.558
She was pretty sure that the Whales could beat the Bobcats, but the Terriers were the best team in the league; it would take more than the team's usual plays to beat them.

14
00:01:48.559 --> 00:01:55.954
If Dirk would only practice some of Brooklyn's plays, the team might have a shot at winning the final championship game.

15
00:01:55.955 --> 00:02:00.898
She sighed. "I need a study break."

16
00:02:00.899 --> 00:02:09.205
Brooklyn pulled on her Whales sweatshirt and basketball sneakers.

17
00:02:09.206 --> 00:02:16.377
She went downstairs to the family room where her father was reading the Sunday newspaper.

18
00:02:16.378 --> 00:02:22.963
"Dad, can I borrow your laptop?" she asked. "I want to study some basketball videos."

19
00:02:22.964 --> 00:02:29.940
Her father lowered his newspaper. "At lunch you mentioned studying for a history test."

20
00:02:29.941 --> 00:02:34.543
"I promise to study World War II after I review some plays."

21
00:02:34.544 --> 00:02:39.863
"You sure work hard for those Whales." Mr. Robbins smiled.

22
00:02:39.864 --> 00:02:48.690
"I suppose World War II can wait an hour." He pulled his laptop from his briefcase and gave it to Brooklyn.

23
00:02:48.691 --> 00:02:50.738
"Please be careful with this."

24
00:02:50.739 --> 00:02:56.272
"I will. I promise," Brooklyn said. "Thanks, Dad."

25
00:02:56.273 --> 00:03:00.890
She took the computer from her father and gripped it in her hands.

26
00:03:00.891 --> 00:03:05.583
She pretended she had glue on her fingers so she wouldn't drop it.

27
00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:16.739
Brooklyn went through the kitchen and headed to the garage. Mrs. Robbins was stirring a large pot of chili on the stove.

28
00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:21.993
"Mom, would you open the door for me, please? I'm going outside to practice."

29
00:03:21.994 --> 00:03:31.475
"Sure, sweetie." Her mom wiped her hands on a towel. Her eyes widened at the sight of the computer in Brooklyn's hands.

30
00:03:31.476 --> 00:03:34.967
"You're not playing basketball with Dad's computer!"

31
00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:40.303
"I'm studying some professional and college plays so I can try them out with the Whales."

32
00:03:40.304 --> 00:03:49.981
"Oh. I see." Brooklyn's mom opened the kitchen door and followed her into the garage.

33
00:03:49.982 --> 00:03:56.878
She pressed the button to open the big door.

34
00:03:56.879 --> 00:04:05.362
The sun shone brightly in the sky, but the March air chilled Brooklyn's fingers.

35
00:04:05.363 --> 00:04:14.457
"Here, Brooklyn. Use this for the laptop." Mrs. Robbins carried out a folding beach chair from the garage.

36
00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:19.507
She placed it several yards away from the basketball hoop.

37
00:04:19.508 --> 00:04:26.849
"Okay." Brooklyn set the laptop on the chair and ran back into the garage.

38
00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:34.928
She picked up her favorite basketball—a red, white, and blue one that had been a birthday gift last year.

39
00:04:34.929 --> 00:04:41.024
Mrs. Robbins rubbed her hands. "When you're finished, come in for some chili.

40
00:04:41.025 --> 00:04:45.595
I'll close the garage door so the basketball doesn't hit the car."

41
00:04:45.596 --> 00:04:54.317
"Good idea. Thanks, Mom." Brooklyn clicked the keyboard. First she wanted to watch the video with the loop play.

42
00:04:54.318 --> 00:04:58.325
Maybe she could figure out where it had gone wrong for the Whales.

43
00:04:58.326 --> 00:05:03.160
The more Brooklyn watched the loop-play video, the more excited she got.

44
00:05:03.161 --> 00:05:08.153
The Whales had missed one critical pass in the game versus the Terriers.

45
00:05:08.154 --> 00:05:14.307
If Brooklyn and Marv practiced the loop play with the players, the team could try it again in the next game!

46
00:05:14.308 --> 00:05:23.536
"This time it'll work!" Brooklyn declared. She began dribbling the basketball to warm up.

47
00:05:23.537 --> 00:05:31.965
Just then a rider on a blue bicycle turned into Brooklyn's driveway. "Hi, Brooklyn."

48
00:05:31.966 --> 00:05:34.443
"Hey, Jacey," Brooklyn said.

49
00:05:34.444 --> 00:05:37.377
"Want to ride to the park?" Jacey asked.

50
00:05:37.378 --> 00:05:43.548
Brooklyn shook her head, a little surprised that Jacey was suddenly being friendly to her.

51
00:05:43.549 --> 00:05:48.865
"I'm working on my coaching. I know what went wrong in the game against the Terriers."

52
00:05:48.866 --> 00:05:55.611
"Me too!" Jacey laughed loudly. "You fell and Coach broke his rear!"

53
00:05:55.612 --> 00:06:00.378
"Very funny." Brooklyn took a shot at the hoop.

54
00:06:00.379 --> 00:06:13.597
The ball hit the rim and bounced toward Jacey, who quickly parked her bike and ran after the ball.

55
00:06:13.598 --> 00:06:18.010
"We missed a key pass during the loop play," Brooklyn went on.

56
00:06:18.011 --> 00:06:21.179
"The guard has to wait before going to the net.

57
00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:28.671
The loop play might have worked if Dirk had stayed at center court. I'll teach the play again at practice tomorrow."

58
00:06:28.672 --> 00:06:34.063
"Dirk won't do it," Jacey said, passing the ball.

59
00:06:34.064 --> 00:06:38.917
"If it helps the team win, he will," Brooklyn said confidently.

60
00:06:38.918 --> 00:06:42.770
Jacey shrugged. "I'm not so sure about that."

61
00:06:42.771 --> 00:06:48.157
They dribbled the ball back and forth.

62
00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:54.575
Each girl tried shots from different spots on the driveway.

63
00:06:54.576 --> 00:06:59.416
Then Jacey stopped playing, holding the ball on her hip.

64
00:06:59.417 --> 00:07:05.819
"Brooklyn, don't take this the wrong way. But it's not just Dirk who's bothered by your coaching.

65
00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:09.303
Some players think you're acting like a know-it-all."

66
00:07:09.304 --> 00:07:14.702
Brooklyn's face grew hot. "I'm acting like a know-it-all?" she thought.

67
00:07:14.703 --> 00:07:21.630
She was just trying to help Marv while Coach was recovering. "Do you think that, Jacey?" she asked.

68
00:07:21.631 --> 00:07:30.781
Jacey glanced at the ground. "I know you love basketball, but that doesn't mean you're an expert. You don't even play for the team."

69
00:07:30.782 --> 00:07:41.532
Brooklyn felt her heart pounding. "I only want to help the team win. The Whales could be the league champions."

70
00:07:41.533 --> 00:07:45.865
"Well, you're getting on the players' nerves," Jacey said.

71
00:07:45.866 --> 00:07:49.375
"I'm your friend, so I thought you should know."

72
00:07:49.376 --> 00:07:57.185
Brooklyn swallowed, unsure what to say. Then she did the only thing that helped when she was upset.

73
00:07:57.186 --> 00:08:04.985
She grabbed her basketball from Jacey and began dribbling.

74
00:08:04.986 --> 00:08:15.582
She dribbled faster, tuning out Jacey for a moment. Marv often said he listened to his gut when deciding plays.

75
00:08:15.583 --> 00:08:22.096
Brooklyn didn't want to annoy anyone, but she knew in her gut that she could help the team.

76
00:08:22.097 --> 00:08:28.087
"Okay, Jacey," she said finally. "Thanks for the advice. Now watch this!"

77
00:08:28.088 --> 00:08:39.973
Brooklyn tossed the ball high, hoping for a clean shot through the basket. Instead the ball hit the rim and bounced wide.

78
00:08:39.974 --> 00:08:45.718
"No!" Brooklyn cried. She ran, but she was too late.

79
00:08:45.719 --> 00:09:00.368
The basketball came down, smashing into the beach chair. Her dad's laptop crashed to the ground.
